  "output": "Now I have a full picture. Here's the complete performance analysis:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis\n\n### 1. Domain Lock Held During Sleep — Critical Bottleneck\n\n**File:** `src/fetch/engine.py:79-87`\n\n`asyncio.sleep` is awaited while holding `_domain_lock`, so all concurrent batch fetches are serialized behind this lock. If one domain needs a 900ms delay, no other domain's timing can even be checked.\n\n```python\n# CURRENT — lock held across sleep, serializes all domains\nasync with self._domain_lock:\n    delay_required = 1.0 - (time.time() - last_request)\n    if delay_required > 0:\n        await asyncio.sleep(delay_required)   # ← holds lock here\n    self._domain_last_request[domain] = time.time()\n\n# FIX — release lock before sleeping\nwhile True:\n    async with self._domain_lock:\n        elapsed = time.time() - self._domain_last_request[domain]\n        if elapsed >= 1.0:\n            self._domain_last_request[domain] = time.time()\n            break\n        delay = 1.0 - elapsed\n    await asyncio.sleep(delay)              # ← lock released\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. N+1 Connection Pattern — Database\n\n**File:** `src/data/db.py:82-368`\n\nEvery method opens and closes its own `aiosqlite` connection. A single query triggers at least 5 sequential connection open/close cycles: `save_query` (initial), `save_agent_response` × N, `save_orchestrator_response`, `save_query` (update). SQLite connection setup has non-trivial overhead with WAL mode negotiation on each open.\n\n```python\n# CURRENT — new connection per operation\nasync def save_query(self, record: QueryRecord) -> None:\n    async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db_path) as db:  # open\n        await db.execute(...)\n        await db.commit()\n    # close\n\n# FIX — persistent connection (added to DatabaseManager)\nclass DatabaseManager:\n    def __init__(self, db_path: Path = _DB_PATH) -> None:\n        self._db_path = db_path\n        self._db_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        self._db: aiosqlite.Connection | None = None\n\n    async def _get_db(self) -> aiosqlite.Connection:\n        if self._db is None:\n            self._db = await aiosqlite.connect(self._db_path)\n            self._db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n            await self._db.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL\")\n        return self._db\n\n    async def save_query(self, record: QueryRecord) -> None:\n        db = await self._get_db()\n        await db.execute(\"INSERT OR REPLACE INTO queries ...\", (...))\n        await db.commit()\n\n    async def close(self) -> None:\n        if self._db:\n            await self._db.close()\n            self._db = None\n```\n\nWire `close()` into the FastAPI shutdown lifespan.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Regex Compiled Inside Hot Path\n\n**File:** `src/fetch/engine.py:69-71`\n\n`import re` and regex construction run on every call to `_normalize_url()`, which is called on every `fetch()`. Both should be module-level constants.\n\n```python\n# CURRENT\ndef _normalize_url(self, url: str) -> str:\n    import re\n    if re.search(r'laws-lois\\.justice\\.gc\\.ca/eng/acts/[^/]+/$', url):\n        ...\n\n# FIX — module level\nimport re\n_LAWS_LOIS_RE = re.compile(r'laws-lois\\.justice\\.gc\\.ca/eng/acts/[^/]+/$')\n\nclass FetchEngine:\n    def _normalize_url(self, url: str) -> str:\n        if _LAWS_LOIS_RE.search(url):\n            return url.rstrip('/') + '/FullText.html'\n        return url\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. GenerativeModel Instantiated Per LLM Call\n\n**File:** `src/llm/client.py:40-50`\n\n`_make_model()` constructs a new `genai.GenerativeModel` on every `chat()`, `stream_chat()`, and `chat_parsed()` call. For a query that hits 4–8 specialists plus routing and synthesis, that's 6–10 model constructions.\n\n```python\n# CURRENT\nasync def chat(self, system_prompt: str, user_message: str, model: str | None = None) -> str:\n    m = self._make_model(model)   # ← new object every call\n    ...\n\n# FIX — cache keyed by (name, json_output)\ndef __init__(self) -> None:\n    ...\n    self._model_cache: dict[tuple[str, bool], genai.GenerativeModel] = {}\n\ndef _make_model(self, model: str | None = None, json_output: bool = False) -> genai.GenerativeModel:\n    key = (model or self._model_name, json_output)\n    if key not in self._model_cache:\n        generation_config = {\n            \"temperature\": self._config.model.temperature,\n            \"top_p\": self._config.model.top_p,\n        }\n        if json_output:\n            generation_config[\"response_mime_type\"] = \"application/json\"\n        self._model_cache[key] = genai.GenerativeModel(\n            model_name=key[0], generation_config=generation_config\n        )\n    return self._model_cache[key]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Policy Registry Read 8 Times at Startup\n\n**File:** `src/agents/specialist.py:72-75`\n\nEach of the 8 `SpecialistAgent` instances calls `_load_instruments()`, which opens, reads, and JSON-parses `policy_registry.json` independently.\n\n```python\n# CURRENT — 8 disk reads\ndef _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n    with open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:\n        registry = json.load(f)\n    return [r for r in registry if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n\n# FIX — read once at module level\n_REGISTRY: list[dict] = json.loads(_REGISTRY_PATH.read_text())\n\nclass SpecialistAgent(GenericAgent):\n    def _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n        return [r for r in _REGISTRY if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Citations Parsed from LLM JSON Then Immediately Discarded\n\n**File:** `src/agents/orchestrator.py:151-153`\n\n`OrchestratorResponse(**parsed)` populates `citations` from the LLM's JSON output, then line 153 overwrites it with `_aggregate_citations`. The JSON deserialization of the LLM's citation array is wasted.\n\n```python\n# CURRENT\norch_response = OrchestratorResponse(**parsed)\norch_response.citations = self._aggregate_citations(specialist_responses)\n\n# FIX — skip populating citations from LLM JSON\nparsed_without_citations = {k: v for k, v in parsed.items() if k != \"citations\"}\norch_response = OrchestratorResponse(**parsed_without_citations, citations=[])\norch_response.citations = self._aggregate_citations(specialist_responses)\n```\n\nOr better — exclude `citations` from the structured JSON the LLM is asked to produce, since it's always overridden.\n\n---\n\n### 7. `_get_default_ttl` Reconstructs Lists on Every Call\n\n**File:** `src/fetch/cache.py:99-110`\n\nTwo lists are created on every TTL lookup, which happens on every cache store operation.\n\n```python\n# CURRENT\ndef _get_default_ttl(self, url: str) -> int:\n    legislation_domains = [\"laws-lois.justice.gc.ca\"]\n    collective_domains = [\"tbs-sct.canada.ca/agreements-conventions\", ...]\n    ...\n\n# FIX — class constants\nclass FetchCache:\n    _LEGISLATION_DOMAINS = (\"laws-lois.justice.gc.ca\",)\n    _COLLECTIVE_DOMAINS = (\n        \"tbs-sct.canada.ca/agreements-conventions\",\n        \"www.njc-cnm.gc.ca/s14\",\n    )\n\n    def _get_default_ttl(self, url: str) -> int:\n        if any(d in url for d in self._LEGISLATION_DOMAINS):\n            return 720\n        if any(d in url for d in self._COLLECTIVE_DOMAINS):\n            return 720\n        return self._config.cache.ttl_hours\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. `content_hash` Recomputed on Every Property Access\n\n**File:** `src/fetch/cache.py:37-38`\n\nThe `CacheEntry.content_hash` property runs `sha256` on potentially large content strings on every access. It's accessed at least once per cache write.\n\n```python\n# CURRENT\n@property\ndef content_hash(self) -> str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(self.content.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n# FIX — compute once via __post_init__ (convert to dataclass with field)\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\n@dataclass\nclass CacheEntry:\n    url: str\n    content: str\n    ttl_hours: int\n    status_code: int | None = None\n    content_length: int | None = None\n    _hash: str = field(init=False, repr=False, compare=False)\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        self._hash = hashlib.sha256(self.content.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n    @property\n    def content_hash(self) -> str:\n        return self._hash\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. Frontend: DOM Query on Every Keypress\n\n**File:** `static/js/app.js:62-65`\n\n`isProcessing()` queries the DOM (`querySelector`) on every `input` event, which fires continuously while typing.\n\n```javascript\n// CURRENT — DOM query per keypress\nqueryInput.addEventListener('input', () => {\n    const hasText = queryInput.value.trim().length > 0;\n    sendButton.disabled = !hasText || isProcessing();  // ← DOM query\n});\n\nfunction isProcessing() {\n    return !!currentQueryId &&\n           agentList.querySelector('.status-dot[data-status=\"working\"]') !== null;\n}\n\n// FIX — track with a boolean state variable\nlet _processingActive = false;\n\nfunction setProcessing(active) {\n    _processingActive = active;\n}\n\nfunction isProcessing() {\n    return _processingActive;\n}\n\n// Set true when query starts, false in resetProcessingState()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10. Frontend: DOM Traversal on Every Streaming Chunk\n\n**File:** `static/js/app.js:173-183`\n\n`handleResponseChunk` calls `chatHistory.querySelector('.message.system:last-of-type')` on every chunk received. Cache the reference after the element is created.\n\n```javascript\n// CURRENT — querySelector per chunk\nfunction handleResponseChunk(data) {\n    let messageEl = chatHistory.querySelector('.message.system:last-of-type');\n    if (!messageEl) {\n        messageEl = createMessage('system', '', currentQueryId);\n        chatHistory.appendChild(messageEl);\n    }\n    ...\n}\n\n// FIX — module-level ref, cleared per query\nlet _activeMessageEl = null;\n\nfunction handleResponseChunk(data) {\n    if (!_activeMessageEl) {\n        _activeMessageEl = createMessage('system', '', currentQueryId);\n        chatHistory.appendChild(_activeMessageEl);\n    }\n    _activeMessageEl.querySelector('.message-text').textContent += data.chunk;\n    scrollToBottom();\n}\n\n// Clear in resetProcessingState():\nfunction resetProcessingState() {\n    _activeMessageEl = null;\n    ...\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 11. Routing LLM Call Uses Full Synthesis System Prompt\n\n**File:** `src/agents/orchestrator.py:287-298`\n\n`_route()` sends the full 87-line `ORCHESTRATOR_PROMPT` (written for synthesis) as the system prompt for what is purely a routing decision. This sends unnecessary tokens to the API on every query.\n\n```python\n_ROUTING_PROMPT = (\n    \"You are a query router for a federal HR policy advisory system. \"\n    \"Select which specialist agents to consult and formulate focused sub-queries. \"\n    \"Respond with ONLY a valid JSON object, no other text.\"\n)\n\nasync def _route(self, query_text: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    raw = await self._llm_client.chat(\n        system_prompt=_ROUTING_PROMPT,   # ← shorter, purpose-fit prompt\n        user_message=routing_request,\n    )\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority Summary\n\n| Priority | Issue | File | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **High** | Domain lock held during sleep | `engine.py:79-84` | Serializes all concurrent fetches |\n| **High** | N+1 DB connections | `db.py` | 5+ connection opens per query |\n| **Medium** | `GenerativeModel` recreated per call | `llm/client.py:40` | Object overhead × 6-10 per query |\n| **Medium** | Routing uses full synthesis prompt | `orchestrator.py:300` | Unnecessary token cost |\n| **Medium** | Regex compiled on every `fetch()` | `engine.py:69` | Import + compile per URL |\n| **Low** | Policy registry read 8× at startup | `specialist.py:72` | One-time but avoidable |\n| **Low** | `content_hash` recomputed on access | `cache.py:38` | CPU waste on large docs |\n| **Low** | TTL lists rebuilt per cache store | `cache.py:99` | Minor allocation churn |\n| **Low** | DOM query per keypress | `app.js:64` | Minor jank while typing |\n| **Low** | DOM traversal per streaming chunk | `app.js:173` | Minor (streaming not used yet) |\n\nThe domain lock bug and the N+1 connection pattern are the two changes with the most real-world impact given how the system currently runs.\n",
